Content shell: new windows to the embedder.

What a page opens in a new window (window.open, a link with
target=_blank) the content shell opens as a window of its own. zebkit's
application decides instead (zebkit_view_on_new_window()): an embedder's
handler gets the URL first, and when it takes it no window is made, for
window.open (IsWebContentsCreationOverridden) and for links
(OpenURLFromTab).

--- a/content/shell/browser/shell.cc
+++ b/content/shell/browser/shell.cc
@@ -156,6 +156,28 @@ void Shell::QuitMainMessageLoopForTesting() {
 }
 
 // static
+namespace {
+Shell::NewWindowHandler& NewWindowHandlerForEmbedder() {
+  static base::NoDestructor<Shell::NewWindowHandler> handler;
+  return *handler;
+}
+}  // namespace
+
+void Shell::SetNewWindowHandler(NewWindowHandler handler) {
+  NewWindowHandlerForEmbedder() = std::move(handler);
+}
+
+bool Shell::IsWebContentsCreationOverridden(
+    RenderFrameHost* opener,
+    SiteInstance* source_site_instance,
+    mojom::WindowContainerType window_container_type,
+    const GURL& opener_url,
+    const std::string& frame_name,
+    const GURL& target_url) {
+  const NewWindowHandler& handler = NewWindowHandlerForEmbedder();
+  return handler && handler.Run(web_contents(), target_url);
+}
+
